{
  "version": 34,
  "issued_at": "2026-08-10T15:30:00Z",
  "comment": "Policy 34. Points app_update at drawbridge 0.2.6 (version_code 17), signed after the assets were published and verified to hash to their pin. Back to a versioned URL rather than /releases/latest/download/, for the reason policies 27 to 30 used one: v0.2.6 is a DPC-only pre-release and must not become latest, because it carries no herald assets and every required_apps URL would 404 on every device the moment it did. v0.2.5 stays latest, so required_apps and the QR keep resolving from it. What 0.2.6 changes is the delivery channel itself: USB debugging now follows the lock rather than protectedSince, so a phone that has been unlocked with the parent's key hands the cable back and can be given a new drawbridge over it. That matters because nothing else can -- Play Protect refuses this package, so no device installs its own update, and before this the cable was available exactly once, before the first lock. Note the pin is honest but inert on the one provisioned phone: it already runs a version_code 17 build, so app_update sees nothing newer and does nothing.",
